  ('flashbots-searcher-infrastructure', 'Flashbots (Searcher Infrastructure)', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'mev-block-builders', 'https://docs.flashbots.net/', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "The primary infrastructure through which MEV searchers submit bundles that are evaluated and ordered by block builders.", "extras": {"Block Construction Authority": "Partial (bundles only; no full block construction)", "Censorship or Filtering Policies": "Policy-dependent (historically OFAC-aligned via relay interfaces; evolving)", "Estimated Validator Coverage": "Large (via dominant builder/relay adoption)", "Governance Influence Vector": "Corporate + Ecosystem norms", "Infrastructure Control": "Centralized (core infrastructure with open participation)", "MEV Subsector Type": "Searcher Infrastructure (Block-Coupled)", "Operational Role": "Provides the dominant bundle submission pipeline used by searchers to deliver ordered transaction bundles directly into builder workflows.", "Practitioner Validation Check": "If Flashbots’ searcher infrastructure disappeared, builder pipelines would fragment and a large share of structured MEV would temporarily fail to reach blocks.", "Practitioner’s Note": "Flashbots’ searcher pipeline set the standard for bundle-based MEV; many competing systems remain interoperable with its formats.", "Primary MEV Types Enabled": "Arbitrage, liquidations, backrunning, bundle-based MEV", "Protocol Influence Surface": "High (bundle format standards, MEV-Boost norms)", "Reason for Inclusion": "- Generates bundles that directly shape block contents\n- Feeds builders at the protocol boundary\n- Materially influences ordering outcomes pre-finalization", "Single-Point-of-Failure Risk": "High", "Transaction Ordering Control": "Conditional (ordering within bundles; relative priority via builder selection)", "Validator Access Path": "Indirect via builders and relays (MEV-Boost ecosystem)", "Vertical Integration Flag": "Yes (searcher infra + bui